course: dictionary
lesson: 10504
title: The number twenty
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Twenty is a number. Written with digits it is 20, and it is two tens. When you count in tens (10, 20, 30), twenty is the second stop.
explain: You can make twenty in other ways too. Four lots of five make twenty, so 4 × 5 = 20. Finding more than one way to reach the same number helps you check your answers.
explain: Twenty also turns up in everyday talk. «Picture one wet bus stop with the bus twenty minutes late» uses twenty to mean a length of time, not a count of things. Ages work the same way: a person «in her twenties» is somewhere between 20 and 29.
fact: Twenty is written as 20 and means two tens.
fact: Four fives make twenty: 4 × 5 = 20.
fact: A twenty is a twenty-pound note, so the change from a twenty is 20 minus the cost.
fact: «Quatre-vingts» is French for 80, word for word four twenties.
exercise: What is two tens? | Twelve | *Twenty | Two | Two hundred
exercise: Ruby pays with a twenty-pound note for a book that costs £12. How much change should she get? | £2 | £32 | *£8 | £12
exercise: Find the word in «Picture one wet bus stop with the bus twenty minutes late» that is a number. | bus | *twenty | stop | wet
test: What is 4 × 5? | 45 | 9 | 54 | *20
test: Count in tens: 10, 20, 30, what comes next? | *40 | 31 | 50 | 35
exam: A girl is «in her twenties». What age could she be? | 200 or more | Between 2 and 9 | Exactly 2 | *Between 20 and 29
